>INFO

    MAXINFO=1000

    EXCERPT FIXTURE. The HEAD and DEFINEMEAS blocks and both MTSECT sections below
    are cut verbatim from a custodian file of the GSSA Roxby Downs MT 2018
    open-file release (Geological Survey of South Australia, released for BHP),
    served in the AusMT corpus as
    surveys/roxby-downs-2018/transfer_functions/edi/53(RR).edi.

    TWO EDITS, both stated so nothing here is taken for the custodian's file: this
    INFO block replaces the source's EPI-KIT JSON block; and every data block is
    truncated to its first seven frequencies, with NFREQ and the block comment
    counts restated to match. No value is altered, and the DATAID is the
    custodian's own.

    The DATAID is what this fixture is for. mt_metadata 1.0.10's
    validate_station_name rewrites space, hyphen, full stop and plus to
    underscore and then requires the result to match the letters, digits and
    underscore charset; the parentheses survive that rewrite and the read raises,
    so the station never reaches the catalogue at all. Nine of the 764 files in
    that release carry such a DATAID. The file also carries the EPI-KIT section
    stack (here the averaged solution of record and the first realisation),
    because in this release the two defects arrive together.

    No angle bracket appears in this block on purpose: mt_metadata's DEFINEMEAS
    scanner keys on the two-character sequence anywhere in a line, INFO block
    included, and would read this prose as measurement metadata.

>=DEFINEMEAS

